# Fullstack standards

- TypeScript strict; no `any` unless justified in a one-line comment.
- Colocate UI by feature; keep shared primitives thin.
- Server/API boundaries: validate inputs at the edge; never trust client prices.
- Prefer derived state over duplicated state (cart totals from line items).
- Errors: typed results or thrown domain errors — no empty `catch {}`.
- Env: only via `.env.example` keys; never hardcode secrets or payment keys.
- Commits: conventional (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`); small focused diffs.
- Before merge: typecheck + lint + one browser pass on RTL mobile width.
